<title>NEW ZEALAND: CRICKET-NEW ZEALAND A BEAT ENGLAND BY 90 RUNS.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-NEW ZEALAND A BEAT ENGLAND BY 90 RUNS.</headline>
<dateline>WANGANUI, New Zealand 1997-02-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>New Zealand A dismissed England for 272 on the last morning of their four-day match to win by 90 runs on Sunday.</p>
<p>Scores:</p>
<p>New Zealand A first innings 181 (M. Horne 64, C. Silverwood 6-44) and 288 (L.Howell 66. A.Caddick 3-52).</p>
<p>England first innings 107 (R. Irani 40, G. Allott 4-44, H. Davis 4-22) and 272 (N.Hussain 57, J.Russell 61 not out, R.Croft 49. G.Allott 4-76)</p>
</text>
